{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FINAL REBAR-DEBUG REPORT (2026-08-09)\n\nProblem: whitespace-only edits to `no_file_impact_reason` changed signed plan-review material and returned `stale-material`, contrary to the original whitespace-normalization invariant.\n\nProven root cause: `material_basis()` canonicalized the description but inserted the no-file-impact reason byte-for-byte for scope `none`; `material_fingerprint()` faithfully serialized and hashed that first divergence. Fixed-context runtime fingerprints split for `docs only`, `docs only `, `docs only\\n`, and `\\ndocs only`, while normalizing only the reason restored the baseline exactly. Scope/serializer/legacy-dispatch rivals were rejected. Authority: parent `unspirited-polished-arcticfox`, `material_diff.py` canonicalization contract, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md` material-staleness contract.\n\nTest: `tests/unit/plan_review/test_callous_reason_whitespace.py` is an in-process oracle through real material hashing and `compute_validity`, mocking only store/signature boundaries. Its final form was observed RED before the fix (4 expected failures: three unequal whitespace fingerprints plus a whitespace-only review reading stale; 6 controls passed). After the held-out production fix it was GREEN 10/10. Reintroducing the exact raw-reason insertion returned the same 4 failures; restoring the fix returned GREEN 10/10. The test asserts observable fingerprints/verdicts, so formatting/refactoring does not invalidate it.\n\nFix: Gerrit change 1565, merged as `b6c05c87b6b24b6bf66026e8589f54d810445562`. An independent `normalize_reason=True` switch now flows through `material_basis` -> `material_fingerprint` -> `current_material_fingerprint_impl`. Current reasons reuse `normalize_insignificant_whitespace`. `_legacy_material_ok` explicitly disables reason normalization in the pre-330c and post-330c/pre-2be7 candidates and adds the post-2be7/pre-fix canonical-description/raw-reason candidate.\n\nScope and safety: caller sweep found only fingerprint/component consumers; none depends behaviorally on cosmetic reason bytes. Historical byte-exact recomputation is preserved explicitly. This restores documented behavior, adds no dependency, weakens no test, and leaves all edited production modules below the 800-line limit. Local gates: held-out 10 passed; focused plan-review/legacy 185 passed; `make check` passed. Local `rebar review-code`: PASS, 0 findings; independent reviewer: APPROVE, 0 findings. Gerrit: `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`; full CI matrix succeeded on Linux Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS Python 3.13, including default and integration tiers.\n\nSiblings/parity: construct sweep of the material basis found exactly two free-text fields: description and no-file-impact reason; both now use the same insignificant-whitespace canonicalizer, so no additional raw free-text sibling remains. Parity rule: current plan-review free text ignores only boundary/trailing whitespace while meaningful edits remain material. CLI review/status/gates, MCP `review_plan`, the library facade, automated close/review workflows, and both generation/validation directions all converge on the shared material basis; no MISSING surface.\n\nReplication: the original scenario now certifies for trailing/boundary whitespace variants. Interior whitespace, word changes, scope changes, and an unrelated valid-looking 16-hex fingerprint still return `stale-material`. All three historical raw-reason generations certify unchanged.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: none observed in the fixed seam. The explicit three-generation regression matrix prevents future canonicalization changes from silently invalidating old attestations. Per session directive, this ticket is intentionally left `in_progress` and was not closed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786302173761859001,"uuid":"46338816-93f9-4b7f-bcd6-6261ce367ee9"}